        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Vectors \\(\\vec a\\) and \\(\\vec b\\) have magnitudes \\(3\\) and \\(4\\), respectively, and the angle between them is \\(60^\\circ\\). Find \\(\\lvert\\vec a-\\vec b\\rvert\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Using the scalar-product identity, \\(\\lvert\\vec a-\\vec b\\rvert^2=\\lvert\\vec a\\rvert^2+\\lvert\\vec b\\rvert^2-2\\lvert\\vec a\\rvert\\lvert\\vec b\\rvert\\cos60^\\circ=9+16-12=13\\). Therefore, \\(\\lvert\\vec a-\\vec b\\rvert=\\sqrt{13}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 112,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
            "creatorId": null,
            "classLevel": "Class 12",
